# --- Source storage model (decided 2026-06-01, "Option B") ---
# Source REPOS are kept as live local clones (with their .git, so we can `git pull`)
# but are NOT committed into the wiki — they're large and reconstructable. The wiki
# tracks only their .md citation pages; `sources/clone-all.sh` rebuilds the clones
# from `sources/repos.manifest.tsv`, pinned to the cited commit.
#
# Captured ARTICLE / PAPER / DOCS snapshots (a single snapshot.md + assets) DO stay
# committed — they're immutable evidence with no upstream to clone.
#
# When you ingest a new repo: add its dir below AND a row to repos.manifest.tsv.

sources/anthropic--skills/
sources/anthropic--financial-services/
sources/garrytan--gstack/
sources/garrytan--gbrain/
sources/every--compound-engineering-plugin/
sources/openai--plugins/
sources/sidneyswift--skills/
sources/mattpocock--skills/
sources/forward-future--loop-library/
sources/vercel--eve/
sources/SHL0MS--skill-diffs/

# PURCHASED / PROPRIETARY source (PM OS, prodmgmt.world): the local evidence copy
# lives here for scanning but must NEVER be committed or pushed — it's licensed,
# paid content and this repo is public. Not in repos.manifest.tsv (no public repo
# to re-clone from); rebuild by re-extracting the purchased zips.
sources/prodmgmt-world--pm-os-bundle/
sources/prodmgmt-world--pm-os-cowork/

# Never commit nested .git directories from any clone that isn't listed above.
sources/**/.git/

